{"id": "EUVD-2026-103577", "enisaUuid": "7a0f53a5-1c33-3132-b079-61501c730cf5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv6: do not let ipv6_find_hdr() return an offset past the packet end\n\nipv6_find_hdr() walks the extension header chain, skipping each header by\nthe length that header itself declares.  ipv6_optlen() returns up to 2048,\nand the skip is never checked against skb->len, so the offset stored in\n*offset can point past the end of the packet.\n\nopenvswitch installs that offset as the transport header, and\nupdate_ipv6_checksum() then reads and writes the transport checksum field\nout of bounds:\n\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in inet_proto_csum_replace16+0x445/0x470\n  Read of size 2 at addr ffff88810b754b06 by task ovs_ipv6_oob/629\n  CPU: 4 UID: 1000 PID: 629 Comm: ovs_ipv6_oob Tainted: G N 7.3.0-rc3+ #348\n  Call Trace:\n   inet_proto_csum_replace16+0x445/0x470\n   set_ipv6_addr+0x3dd/0x460\n   do_execute_actions+0x6a3d/0x7c40\n   ovs_execute_actions+0xfd/0x480\n   ovs_packet_cmd_execute+0xc38/0xf20\n   genl_rcv_msg+0x59e/0x870\n   netlink_rcv_skb+0x18b/0x450\n   genl_rcv+0x2d/0x40\n   netlink_unicast+0x6bc/0xa20\n\n  The buggy address belongs to the object at ffff88810b754980\n   which belongs to the cache skbuff_small_head of size 704\n  The buggy address is located 390 bytes inside of\n   freed 704-byte region [ffff88810b754980, ffff88810b754c40)\n\nOther callers use that offset too, so bound it here rather than in one\ncaller.\n\nReject a header whose declared length does not fit in the packet.\nipv6_find_hdr() already fails with -EBADMSG on a malformed chain, so this\nadds no new failure mode.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:17:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:15", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ca96b38730e31357ef4a9d76af1336958ac670d7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/531255de8971c06d5d5986f85fdc2525d707ba71", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/543354c6efb27eae3372a3a9674aeaa2a86e2b2c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc92cb972e86790b8078337ec41015b748b8f8e5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1c70275ca87e769e1a52abc644d61372d8c016cb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1d42828565889632068fbc2983c34d57c66af4e0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4254d5878c320c19961dd0b8e1d0aca4800d8b7d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ee319bd3a0e976af5087cbe59ebc50a66f31d202"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98532", "GHSA-75wf-hf48-gmfv"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0cabac67-9f20-3858-83a8-4e9f12e00a49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "16d56dfa-d2b0-3031-aee3-de3b6a3dc1d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f8f626754ebeca613cf1af2e6f890cfde0e74d5b <543354c6efb27eae3372a3a9674aeaa2a86e2b2c"}, {"id": "1b550025-2769-3c2d-9a73-5ae8da0e9f26", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f8f626754ebeca613cf1af2e6f890cfde0e74d5b <4254d5878c320c19961dd0b8e1d0aca4800d8b7d"}, {"id": "32af7f57-b1b1-3a6c-ba44-02ff7b03c1c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "35196f10-a287-3426-9255-4383e524992b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f8f626754ebeca613cf1af2e6f890cfde0e74d5b <531255de8971c06d5d5986f85fdc2525d707ba71"}, {"id": "5306f0ea-1c69-3253-bd53-dfc0d6ac2cec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6cb60e0f-b706-3ab2-92cf-3cc33b31e478", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "7ccf6796-76d4-35ac-9a79-75ce7140ff64", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "826435b4-cf70-3ce5-b294-d8101e19a12b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": 